+Independent executable comparison. This did not import or execute any mounted
+candidate/source module; it used separately written recurrences and an integer
+ordering/count oracle.
+
+case                    equations  operational  expected  match
+[]                      True       True         True      True
+[0]                     True       True         True      True
+[0, 0]                  True       True         True      True
+[0, 0, 0]               False      False        False     True
+[0, 1, 1, 2]            True       True         True      True
+[0, 1, 1, 1, 2]         False      False        False     True
+[0, 2, 1]               False      False        False     True
+[0, 1, 0]               False      False        False     True
+[1, 1, 2, 2]            True       True         True      True
+[1, 1, 2, 2, 2]         False      False        False     True
+[0, 0, 1, 2, 2, 3]      True       True         True      True
+[4, 3, 3]               False      False        False     True
+
+all_cases_match = True
+
+Counterfactual sensitivity:
+
+- Omitting the sorting conjunct accepts `[0, 2, 1]`; expected result is false.
+- Changing `count > 2` to `count > 3` accepts `[0, 0, 0]`; expected result is false.
+- Resetting rather than incrementing on equality accepts `[0, 0, 0]`; expected result is false.
+- Ignoring the prior Boolean accumulator can turn an already-false sorting result true.
+
+These witnesses show that the sorting conjunct, equality increment, threshold,
+and false-result preservation are all load-bearing rather than vacuous.

