+Counterfactual sensitivity:
+
+- Omitting the sorting conjunct accepts `[0, 2, 1]`; expected result is false.
+- Changing `count > 2` to `count > 3` accepts `[0, 0, 0]`; expected result is false.
+- Resetting rather than incrementing on equality accepts `[0, 0, 0]`; expected result is false.
+- Ignoring the prior Boolean accumulator can turn an already-false sorting result true.
+
+These witnesses show that the sorting conjunct, equality increment, threshold,
+and false-result preservation are all load-bearing rather than vacuous.

